## 💡 What I Learned

This project was an important step in my journey from Machine Learning experimentation to building and deploying a complete end-to-end Machine Learning application.

Throughout the project, I worked on:

- Dataset exploration
- Data preprocessing
- Feature selection
- Feature scaling
- Unsupervised Machine Learning
- K-Means clustering
- Cluster interpretation
- PCA dimensionality reduction
- Interactive data visualization
- Streamlit application development
- Model serialization using Joblib
- Git and GitHub version control
- Dependency management
- Cloud deployment

The project also involved solving several real-world development challenges, including feature mismatches, PCA dimensionality errors, visualization issues, Streamlit UI customization, missing dependencies, and file path problems during cloud deployment.

These challenges helped me understand that building a Machine Learning application involves much more than simply training a model. A successful ML project requires a complete workflow from data preparation and model development to application design, debugging, version control, and deployment.

